The audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants for a Michigan operator's license, reading at a plain-English level, plus newcomers and parents of teen drivers who use the same handbook. This section covers children left unattended in vehicles, air bag safety, the Basic Speed Law and standard Michigan speed limits, construction zones with their speed limits, fines and points, merging in work zones, green-light maintenance vehicles, yielding to and moving over for emergency vehicles, and stopping for school buses. It teaches the default speed limits by road type, how work zones change limits and penalties, what to do for stopped and approaching emergency vehicles, and when to stop for a school bus. It assumes no prior driving knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy, so wording stays concrete, procedural and free of legal jargon throughout.
